Student Project: E-Commerce Sales       Performance Analysis
Assessment Level
Medium–Hard | Professional Interview Assessment
Business Scenario
We are working as a Junior Data Analyst for an e-commerce company. The business team has provided raw order-level sales data and wants to understand revenue performance, order status, product performance, regional trends, and sales representative performance.
The task is to transform the raw data into a structured Analysis Report using Google Sheets.
This assessment evaluates your ability to work with real-world data using formulas, conditional logic, aggregation, Pivot Tables, and business-oriented visualizations.
We are expected to work independently and be prepared to explain the logic behind your calculations and analysis.
Dataset
Use the provided dataset:
E-Commerce Sales Dataset
Do not modify or delete the existing raw data unnecessarily.

 

Task 1: Data Preparation & Business Derivation
Work directly in the Data Sheet containing the raw order-level data.
Add the following derived columns:
1. Total Revenue
Create Column K – Total Revenue.
Calculate the revenue generated by each order:
Total Revenue = Quantity × Unit Price
 
Apply the formula consistently to all applicable records.
2. Order Value Classification
Create Column L – Order Type.
Classify each order based on its Total Revenue:
●	High Value — Total Revenue is greater than or equal to 500
●	Standard Value — Total Revenue is less than 500
Use an appropriate IF-based formula rather than manually entering the values.
3. Data Validation Check
Before moving to the analysis, verify that:
●	The Total Revenue calculation is applied correctly.
●	Every valid order has an Order Type.
●	No formulas have been accidentally replaced with hardcoded values.
●	The derived columns are consistent across the dataset.
Be prepared to explain how you validated your calculations.


